1
00:00:01,418 --> 00:00:03,878
[MARIELA] <i>That devil-spawn father of yours</i>

2
00:00:03,962 --> 00:00:05,922
<i>is together with Billy's aunt!</i>

3
00:00:06,548 --> 00:00:08,091
<i>I'll kill them!</i>

4
00:00:08,174 --> 00:00:10,218
<i>No one's dying, okay?</i>

5
00:00:10,301 --> 00:00:14,639
<i>And most of all,</i>
<i>I don't want you to hurt yourself.</i>

6
00:00:14,723 --> 00:00:17,642
[MARIELA]<i> I won't do it</i>
<i>ever again.</i> [SOBS]

7
00:00:18,309 --> 00:00:20,311
<i>I regret doing it.</i>

8
00:00:20,395 --> 00:00:23,356
<i>It's what caused your sister's death.</i>

9
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:25,608
[BEA] <i>Ma, you have to promise me</i>

10
00:00:26,192 --> 00:00:31,698
<i>that you'll leave our revenge to me.</i>

11
00:00:32,323 --> 00:00:34,034
<i>I will avenge us.</i>

12
00:00:34,117 --> 00:00:38,204
<i>I will avenge us both, okay?</i>

13
00:00:38,288 --> 00:00:39,497
<i>Good evening.</i>

14
00:00:39,581 --> 00:00:40,957
<i>I'll just give you the latest update.</i>

15
00:00:41,041 --> 00:00:45,587
<i>We're still looking for Mariela Mercado</i>
<i>and her daughter, Beatrice.</i>

16
00:00:45,670 --> 00:00:48,757
<i>Authorities reported</i>
<i>no fatalities in the fire</i>

17
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:52,844
<i>that broke out at the home</i>
<i>of LoveList CEO Benilda Cariño.</i>

18
00:00:52,927 --> 00:00:54,929
<i>Her father, Enrico Dominguez, however,</i>

19
00:00:55,013 --> 00:00:56,931
<i>remains in a critical condition</i>

20
00:00:57,015 --> 00:00:59,684
<i>after rescuing his son,</i>
<i>Oliver Cariño,</i>

21
00:00:59,768 --> 00:01:02,228
<i>and a woman identified</i>
<i>as Oliver's guardian,</i>

22
00:01:02,312 --> 00:01:03,354
<i>Precious Amador.</i>

23
00:01:03,438 --> 00:01:05,607
<i>Did you hear what your father did?</i>

24
00:01:05,690 --> 00:01:07,442
<i>Acting like a savior!</i>

25
00:01:07,525 --> 00:01:11,029
<i>He went into the fire</i>
<i>to rescue his illegitimate child</i>

26
00:01:11,112 --> 00:01:12,322
<i>and his mistress!</i>

27
00:01:12,405 --> 00:01:13,865
<i>What about us?</i>

28
00:01:13,948 --> 00:01:15,200
<i>What has he done for us?</i>

29
00:01:15,283 --> 00:01:16,367
<i>Nothing!</i>

30
00:01:17,285 --> 00:01:19,287
[REPORTER] <i>CCTV footage revealed</i>

31
00:01:19,370 --> 00:01:21,289
<i>a woman entering the property</i>

32
00:01:21,372 --> 00:01:23,708
<i>shortly before the fire started.</i>

33
00:01:23,792 --> 00:01:26,920
<i>Police have identified her</i>
<i>as Mariela Mercado.</i>

34
00:01:27,003 --> 00:01:29,130
<i>Mercado is now being sought by the police</i>

35
00:01:29,214 --> 00:01:32,717
<i>and is considered a person of interest</i>
<i>in the investigation.</i>

36
00:01:33,927 --> 00:01:35,929
[MARIELA] <i>Why should I be punished?</i>

37
00:01:36,012 --> 00:01:38,223
<i>They're the ones who should suffer!</i>

38
00:01:38,306 --> 00:01:39,808
<i>Not me!</i>

39
00:01:39,891 --> 00:01:41,851
<i>Not us!</i>

40
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:45,063
[BEA]<i> You're Caloy's friend.</i>
<i>Wilfred, right?</i>

41
00:01:45,647 --> 00:01:47,065
<i>You need a fake passport?</i>

42
00:01:47,732 --> 00:01:49,275
<i>For my mom and me.</i>

43
00:01:49,859 --> 00:01:50,693
<i>600,000.</i>

44
00:01:50,777 --> 00:01:52,445
<i>That's too much, Bea!</i>

45
00:01:53,363 --> 00:01:54,989
<i>I already gave you money.</i>

46
00:01:55,073 --> 00:01:56,491
<i>I already gave you the files.</i>

47
00:01:56,574 --> 00:01:58,743
<i>I did everything you asked me to do!</i>

48
00:01:58,827 --> 00:02:00,703
<i>This is our new deal!</i>

49
00:02:00,787 --> 00:02:04,249
<i>You give me 10 million pesos</i>
<i>cash tomorrow,</i>

50
00:02:04,332 --> 00:02:08,586
<i>or our pictures,</i>
<i>your pictures, it will go viral.</i>

51
00:02:08,670 --> 00:02:09,712
<i>So you choose.</i>

52
00:02:10,588 --> 00:02:15,343
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

53
00:02:35,488 --> 00:02:42,203
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

54
00:02:42,287 --> 00:02:44,080
<i>My big girl is 15 years old now.</i>

55
00:02:44,164 --> 00:02:45,748
<i>Time sure flies, doesn't it?</i>

56
00:02:46,332 --> 00:02:47,458
<i>Happy birthday, my dear.</i>

57
00:02:48,209 --> 00:02:50,712
<i>Happy 18th birthday, my dear!</i>

58
00:02:50,795 --> 00:02:53,631
<i>I can't believe you're 18 already.</i>

59
00:02:53,715 --> 00:02:57,760
<i>I am so proud of you</i>
<i>and your company's success.</i>

60
00:02:58,469 --> 00:03:01,264
<i>I hope LoveList will continue to prosper.</i>

61
00:03:02,223 --> 00:03:04,517
<i>I'm here, cheering you on.</i>

62
00:03:04,601 --> 00:03:09,772
[POIGNANT MUSIC PLAYING]

63
00:03:21,492 --> 00:03:25,288
[SOFT FOOTSTEPS]

64
00:03:25,955 --> 00:03:26,873
[PRECIOUS] Billy.

65
00:03:27,957 --> 00:03:29,876
Did you get your father's medicine?

66
00:03:29,959 --> 00:03:31,210
Yes.

67
00:03:33,171 --> 00:03:34,589
What's that?

68
00:03:40,678 --> 00:03:43,306
- [MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]
- [PAPER RUSTLING]

69
00:03:43,389 --> 00:03:45,475
Enrico's letters?

70
00:03:47,018 --> 00:03:48,603
This is a lot.

71
00:03:49,646 --> 00:03:50,772
Every…

72
00:03:51,522 --> 00:03:52,982
Every Christmas,

73
00:03:54,067 --> 00:03:55,485
graduation,

74
00:03:56,444 --> 00:03:57,612
and birthday.

75
00:03:59,322 --> 00:04:01,574
Oliver has some too, Aunt Precious.

76
00:04:05,870 --> 00:04:08,623
He didn't forget
about us after all, Auntie.

77
00:04:08,706 --> 00:04:14,462
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

78
00:04:17,006 --> 00:04:23,763
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

79
00:05:01,050 --> 00:05:04,804
[ECG MACHINE BEEPING STEADILY]

80
00:05:04,887 --> 00:05:05,847
[ENRICO GRUNTS]

81
00:05:05,930 --> 00:05:09,934
[ECG MACHINE BEEPING STEADILY]

82
00:05:10,518 --> 00:05:11,769
[ENRICO] Dear.

83
00:05:11,853 --> 00:05:13,354
Are you safe?

84
00:05:14,605 --> 00:05:15,440
Dad.

85
00:05:15,523 --> 00:05:20,153
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

86
00:05:20,236 --> 00:05:21,988
How do you feel?

87
00:05:22,071 --> 00:05:26,034
[ECG MACHINE BEEPING]

88
00:05:26,117 --> 00:05:27,910
Thank you, my dear.

89
00:05:27,994 --> 00:05:30,663
Thank you for the opportunity you gave me

90
00:05:32,582 --> 00:05:35,084
to be with your brother.

91
00:05:36,544 --> 00:05:40,548
Thank you for saving Oliver
and Auntie Pres, Dad.

92
00:05:41,841 --> 00:05:43,551
How are they?

93
00:05:44,260 --> 00:05:45,720
They're going to be fine.

94
00:05:47,847 --> 00:05:49,265
Don't worry.

95
00:05:50,224 --> 00:05:55,980
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

96
00:06:06,324 --> 00:06:08,910
I saw that you smiled at your father.

97
00:06:11,287 --> 00:06:13,456
You know, it is a big deal for him.

98
00:06:17,168 --> 00:06:21,089
What he did was no joke,
saving you and Oliver.

99
00:06:22,048 --> 00:06:25,802
My father almost died because
of the fire, Auntie Pres.

100
00:06:27,345 --> 00:06:28,387
That's too much.

101
00:06:29,722 --> 00:06:30,807
That's too much.

102
00:06:31,557 --> 00:06:36,312
[PHONE RINGING]

103
00:06:37,897 --> 00:06:39,065
Jordan?

104
00:06:39,148 --> 00:06:44,987
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

105
00:06:45,071 --> 00:06:46,405
Hello?

106
00:06:46,489 --> 00:06:47,657
[JORDAN] <i>Dude?</i>

107
00:06:47,740 --> 00:06:49,742
<i>I'm here at your house.</i>

108
00:06:50,785 --> 00:06:52,620
<i>They've recovered some of your things.</i>

109
00:06:53,329 --> 00:06:54,580
<i>Would you like to see?</i>

110
00:06:56,374 --> 00:06:57,708
Okay.

111
00:06:57,792 --> 00:07:04,757
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

112
00:07:15,184 --> 00:07:19,355
[KEYBOARD CLACKING]

113
00:07:20,273 --> 00:07:25,820
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

114
00:07:25,903 --> 00:07:28,823
MIDNIGHT, OKAY? OR ELSE.

115
00:07:37,915 --> 00:07:39,834
How long are we staying here?

116
00:07:43,004 --> 00:07:44,172
Um…

117
00:07:44,881 --> 00:07:47,675
Not long.
We're going to get out of here soon.

118
00:07:48,426 --> 00:07:49,594
How?

119
00:07:49,677 --> 00:07:51,512
[EXHALES SHARPLY] Ma.

120
00:07:52,096 --> 00:07:53,723
I'm making a way, okay?

121
00:07:54,807 --> 00:07:57,768
I'll take care of it. I told you, right?

122
00:07:57,852 --> 00:07:59,312
I won't let you go to jail.

123
00:08:00,354 --> 00:08:01,564
I-I'm sorry, dear.

124
00:08:02,982 --> 00:08:05,443
I've become even more of a burden to you.

125
00:08:06,110 --> 00:08:08,654
Ma. You're my mother.

126
00:08:09,280 --> 00:08:10,156
Okay?

127
00:08:10,239 --> 00:08:12,241
You'll never be a burden to me.

128
00:08:12,325 --> 00:08:14,535
You're the only family I have.

129
00:08:14,619 --> 00:08:15,912
I'd do anything for you.

130
00:08:15,995 --> 00:08:17,205
I'm not.

131
00:08:17,914 --> 00:08:19,373
You still have a father.

132
00:08:20,249 --> 00:08:22,502
The thing is,
we're not important to him anymore.

133
00:08:22,585 --> 00:08:24,879
Is that jerk still alive?

134
00:08:26,881 --> 00:08:33,846
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

135
00:08:40,937 --> 00:08:42,563
[PHONE RINGING]

136
00:08:43,147 --> 00:08:45,441
Hello, Daddy? Yes, I'm on my way.

137
00:08:45,525 --> 00:08:46,609
Are you all right?

138
00:08:46,692 --> 00:08:47,735
Okay, okay.

139
00:08:48,653 --> 00:08:49,779
Bye.

140
00:08:55,993 --> 00:08:57,537
<i>Oh, there.</i>

141
00:08:57,620 --> 00:08:59,455
<i>Your fever has gone down a bit.</i>

142
00:09:00,206 --> 00:09:02,083
<i>But don't leave me yet, Pa.</i>

143
00:09:02,166 --> 00:09:04,835
<i>You might leave again.</i>

144
00:09:05,503 --> 00:09:08,089
<i>Of course I won't leave my baby.</i>

145
00:09:08,172 --> 00:09:10,550
<i>Not until I'm sure that you're all better.</i>

146
00:09:10,633 --> 00:09:12,051
- [LAUGHS]
- [SIGHS CONTENTEDLY]

147
00:09:14,637 --> 00:09:21,602
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

148
00:09:25,606 --> 00:09:28,025
[ELEVATOR DOOR OPENS]

149
00:09:35,074 --> 00:09:37,034
Initially, the medical team thought

150
00:09:37,118 --> 00:09:39,245
diabetes was your preexisting condition.

151
00:09:39,328 --> 00:09:41,998
But upon further evaluation
of your condition,

152
00:09:42,081 --> 00:09:44,875
you are in an advanced stage
of heart failure.

153
00:09:44,959 --> 00:09:47,253
And based on your medical records,

154
00:09:47,336 --> 00:09:49,672
you have maintenance medicines
needed for this.

155
00:09:49,755 --> 00:09:52,049
But, Enrico, this is not enough.

156
00:09:52,133 --> 00:09:54,051
[ECG MACHINE BEEPING]

157
00:09:54,135 --> 00:09:55,636
Doc, have you told my family?

158
00:09:56,512 --> 00:09:57,680
Ah, not yet.

159
00:09:58,806 --> 00:09:59,890
Doc, please.

160
00:10:00,474 --> 00:10:02,059
Don't tell them.

161
00:10:02,143 --> 00:10:04,103
Your family needs to know

162
00:10:04,687 --> 00:10:06,564
that you have arteries that are blocked.

163
00:10:07,189 --> 00:10:09,942
Enrico, you will have to
tell them sooner or later.

164
00:10:10,026 --> 00:10:11,485
You'll need surgery.

165
00:10:12,653 --> 00:10:14,697
That will require a lot of money.

166
00:10:14,780 --> 00:10:16,741
I can't afford that, Doc.

167
00:10:17,325 --> 00:10:20,620
I don't want to be a burden to them.

168
00:10:20,703 --> 00:10:23,247
Well, we don't want
your heart to get overworked,

169
00:10:23,331 --> 00:10:25,458
so I suggest you get some rest.

170
00:10:26,751 --> 00:10:29,879
Let's talk about the procedure tomorrow.

171
00:10:29,962 --> 00:10:33,799
[MELANCHOLY MUSIC PLAYING]

172
00:10:33,883 --> 00:10:35,968
[NURSE] This is for the chest pain.

173
00:10:36,510 --> 00:10:38,346
This will make you a bit drowsy, okay?

174
00:10:38,429 --> 00:10:42,683
[ECG MACHINE BEEPING]

175
00:10:42,767 --> 00:10:43,893
[DOCTOR] Okay.

176
00:10:43,976 --> 00:10:45,645
I'll see you tomorrow, Enrico.

177
00:10:48,939 --> 00:10:55,946
[MELANCHOLY MUSIC CONTINUES]

178
00:11:10,419 --> 00:11:14,382
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

179
00:11:14,965 --> 00:11:18,219
<i>You know, since I already</i>
<i>invested my money,</i>

180
00:11:18,844 --> 00:11:19,929
<i>let's just do it.</i>

181
00:11:20,012 --> 00:11:23,474
<i>Come hell or high water,</i>
<i>we will launch LoveLine.</i>

182
00:11:24,058 --> 00:11:25,518
<i>How?</i>

183
00:11:25,601 --> 00:11:26,936
<i>You no longer have an investor.</i>

184
00:11:27,603 --> 00:11:29,939
<i>I'll pawn the house. Double mortgage!</i>

185
00:11:30,940 --> 00:11:32,024
[FLICKS] <i>You're nuts!</i>

186
00:11:32,108 --> 00:11:34,151
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

187
00:11:34,235 --> 00:11:36,445
<i>What do they say is the best school?</i>

188
00:11:37,029 --> 00:11:38,823
<i>It's there in California!</i>

189
00:11:39,407 --> 00:11:41,242
<i>The University of Kingsley.</i>

190
00:11:41,325 --> 00:11:44,912
<i>That's the best school</i>
<i>for software engineering!</i>

191
00:11:44,995 --> 00:11:47,790
<i>- Hmm!</i>
<i>- But…</i>

192
00:11:47,873 --> 00:11:49,583
<i>It's too expensive.</i>

193
00:11:50,418 --> 00:11:52,044
<i>I could study here too.</i>

194
00:11:52,128 --> 00:11:55,673
<i>There are also many Philippine schools</i>
<i>that offer software engineering.</i>

195
00:11:55,756 --> 00:11:58,759
<i>I have my top three schools I can go to.</i>

196
00:11:58,843 --> 00:12:00,886
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

197
00:12:00,970 --> 00:12:03,431
<i>University of Kingsley.</i>

198
00:12:03,973 --> 00:12:06,809
<i>Noted. Okay, you'll study here.</i>

199
00:12:07,351 --> 00:12:08,769
<i>- Really, Billy?</i>
<i>- Mm-hmm!</i>

200
00:12:08,853 --> 00:12:10,062
<i>- Sure?</i>
<i>- Mm-hmm!</i>

201
00:12:10,146 --> 00:12:12,440
<i>- Promise?</i>
<i>- Promise.</i>

202
00:12:12,523 --> 00:12:16,152
<i>I'm going to study well,</i>
<i>so your efforts won't go to waste.</i>

203
00:12:16,235 --> 00:12:17,319
<i>When I graduate,</i>

204
00:12:17,403 --> 00:12:20,906
<i>you can stop working,</i>
<i>so you can finally rest.</i>

205
00:12:20,990 --> 00:12:24,743
<i>You know I'd do anything for you, right?</i>

206
00:12:24,827 --> 00:12:25,744
<i>That's okay.</i>

207
00:12:25,828 --> 00:12:29,248
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

208
00:12:29,331 --> 00:12:30,875
<i>Don't worry, Billy.</i>

209
00:12:31,417 --> 00:12:33,627
<i>We'll protect each other.</i>

210
00:12:34,962 --> 00:12:36,422
<i>Always.</i>

211
00:12:37,840 --> 00:12:39,091
<i>Oh, enough with the flattery.</i>

212
00:12:39,175 --> 00:12:40,718
<i>- Just help me instead.</i>
<i>- You want that?</i>

213
00:12:40,801 --> 00:12:41,760
<i>You want a hug?</i>

214
00:12:41,844 --> 00:12:43,429
<i>- Sure, hug this.</i>
<i>- Okay.</i>

215
00:12:43,512 --> 00:12:45,764
[BOTH LAUGHING]

216
00:12:45,848 --> 00:12:52,062
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

217
00:13:00,821 --> 00:13:02,740
- [SOFT THUD]
- [SNIFFLES]

218
00:13:07,953 --> 00:13:13,501
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

219
00:13:29,975 --> 00:13:35,648
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

220
00:13:51,956 --> 00:13:58,963
[MUSIC TURNS SUSPENSEFUL]

221
00:14:10,432 --> 00:14:16,063
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

222
00:14:32,246 --> 00:14:39,253
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

223
00:14:54,268 --> 00:14:57,646
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

224
00:14:57,730 --> 00:14:58,939
<i>Pa?</i>

225
00:14:59,023 --> 00:15:00,733
- [FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]
- [CAR DOOR CLOSES]

226
00:15:00,816 --> 00:15:02,443
<i>- Pa!</i>
<i>- Hey.</i>

227
00:15:03,694 --> 00:15:05,029
<i>Mm.</i>

228
00:15:05,905 --> 00:15:07,406
<i>A brand-new car?</i>

229
00:15:07,489 --> 00:15:09,325
<i>Is that ours?</i>

230
00:15:09,408 --> 00:15:10,242
<i>Yes.</i>

231
00:15:10,326 --> 00:15:12,161
<i>Now we can go on as many trips as we want.</i>

232
00:15:12,244 --> 00:15:14,204
<i>You miss your sister, don't you?</i>

233
00:15:14,288 --> 00:15:17,708
<i>Well, now we have a car</i>
<i>to visit her in Manila.</i>

234
00:15:17,791 --> 00:15:19,877
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

235
00:15:19,960 --> 00:15:20,836
<i>Manila?</i>

236
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:22,046
<i>So when are we leaving?</i>

237
00:15:22,129 --> 00:15:23,464
<i>Today!</i>

238
00:15:23,547 --> 00:15:24,673
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

239
00:15:24,757 --> 00:15:26,091
<i>We're going right now?</i>

240
00:15:26,175 --> 00:15:28,093
<i>- Yes, so let's go!</i>
- [STAMMERS]

241
00:15:28,177 --> 00:15:30,054
<i>- Your mother's all dressed up.</i>
<i>- Yeah, she is!</i>

242
00:15:30,137 --> 00:15:32,389
<i>Oh! Okay, I won't bother changing then!</i>

243
00:15:32,473 --> 00:15:34,767
<i>- Here, I brought some clothes.</i>
<i>- Let me help you.</i>

244
00:15:34,850 --> 00:15:36,477
<i>Oh, really? Thanks, Ma!</i>

245
00:15:36,560 --> 00:15:37,853
<i>Oh…</i>

246
00:15:37,937 --> 00:15:38,854
<i>- Ma?</i>
<i>- Hmm?</i>

247
00:15:38,938 --> 00:15:40,648
<i>- Can I take the front seat?</i>
<i>- Nuh-uh.</i>

248
00:15:40,731 --> 00:15:42,024
<i>- You can't.</i>
<i>- Okay then.</i>

249
00:15:42,107 --> 00:15:43,317
<i>You can sit there.</i>

250
00:15:47,905 --> 00:15:49,031
[MARIELA GRUNTS]

251
00:15:51,367 --> 00:15:52,409
<i>Okay?</i>

252
00:15:52,493 --> 00:15:53,786
[ENGINE STARTS]

253
00:15:53,869 --> 00:15:54,870
<i>- Let's go!</i>
<i>- Ready?</i>

254
00:15:54,954 --> 00:15:56,789
<i>- We're ready!</i>
<i>- Where do you want to go?</i>

255
00:15:56,872 --> 00:15:57,790
<i>First stop.</i>

256
00:15:57,873 --> 00:15:58,958
<i>A convenience store.</i>

257
00:15:59,041 --> 00:16:00,751
<i>- Convenience store! Let's go!</i>
<i>- My goodness…</i>

258
00:16:00,834 --> 00:16:07,633
[MONITOR BEEPING]

259
00:16:07,716 --> 00:16:10,260
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

260
00:16:10,344 --> 00:16:12,471
<i>Did you hear what your father did?</i>

261
00:16:12,554 --> 00:16:14,306
<i>Acting like a savior!</i>

262
00:16:14,390 --> 00:16:17,851
<i>He went into the fire</i>
<i>to rescue his illegitimate child</i>

263
00:16:17,935 --> 00:16:19,186
<i>and his mistress!</i>

264
00:16:19,269 --> 00:16:20,729
<i>What about us?</i>

265
00:16:20,813 --> 00:16:22,064
<i>What has he done for us?</i>

266
00:16:22,147 --> 00:16:23,190
<i>Nothing!</i>

267
00:16:23,273 --> 00:16:29,655
[MONITOR BEEPING]

268
00:16:29,738 --> 00:16:32,574
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

269
00:16:32,658 --> 00:16:34,576
[BEA] <i>What Mama did was wrong.</i>

270
00:16:35,911 --> 00:16:38,956
<i>It's your fault she turned out like this.</i>

271
00:16:40,541 --> 00:16:42,126
<i>Because you hurt her.</i>

272
00:16:43,502 --> 00:16:45,045
<i>Left her.</i>

273
00:16:46,547 --> 00:16:48,799
<i>You ruined Mama's life.</i>

274
00:16:48,882 --> 00:16:50,467
<i>Our life.</i>

275
00:16:52,428 --> 00:16:54,388
<i>But I'm also mad at myself.</i>

276
00:16:55,889 --> 00:16:59,184
<i>Because I shouldn't be worried about you.</i>

277
00:17:00,477 --> 00:17:01,895
<i>I shouldn't.</i>

278
00:17:01,979 --> 00:17:08,902
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

279
00:17:08,986 --> 00:17:13,240
[MONITOR BEEPING]

280
00:17:14,867 --> 00:17:15,784
Miss.

281
00:17:17,244 --> 00:17:18,829
We'll do a partial payment.

282
00:17:23,208 --> 00:17:25,502
Billy, you should take this too.

283
00:17:25,586 --> 00:17:28,005
- Here, take it.
- No need, Auntie.

284
00:17:28,088 --> 00:17:30,299
I'll take care of it as long as I can.

285
00:17:35,262 --> 00:17:38,307
[CASHIER] I'm sorry, ma'am.
Your card was declined.

286
00:17:38,390 --> 00:17:40,350
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

287
00:17:40,434 --> 00:17:41,727
[PRECIOUS] Billy…

288
00:17:42,770 --> 00:17:44,438
Okay, miss. Just a minute.

289
00:17:45,105 --> 00:17:47,900
I have another card.
I'll just get it from upstairs.

290
00:17:50,194 --> 00:17:51,445
[BILLY] Let's go.

291
00:17:51,528 --> 00:17:58,243
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

292
00:18:02,331 --> 00:18:03,707
[ELEVATOR RINGS]

293
00:18:18,722 --> 00:18:20,724
[PRECIOUS] Billy? Billy, wait!

294
00:18:20,808 --> 00:18:22,810
- Billy! Billy!
- Bea!

295
00:18:22,893 --> 00:18:24,144
- Bea!
- [PRECIOUS] Nurse!

296
00:18:24,228 --> 00:18:30,025
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

297
00:18:38,283 --> 00:18:42,913
- Billy! Billy!
- Hey, let go of me! Hey!

298
00:18:42,996 --> 00:18:44,665
- How dare you show up here?!
- [GROANS]

299
00:18:44,748 --> 00:18:48,252
Why?! You want to make sure
that we're dead, huh?!

300
00:18:48,752 --> 00:18:50,129
What are you talking about?!

301
00:18:50,212 --> 00:18:52,256
- I'm not an idiot!
- [SLAPS]

302
00:18:52,840 --> 00:18:56,468
Your mother's face was seen clearly
on the CCTV footage.

303
00:18:57,511 --> 00:18:59,138
And you're blaming me
for what happened?

304
00:18:59,221 --> 00:19:00,889
Every single bad thing
going on in your life,

305
00:19:00,973 --> 00:19:02,141
you'll blame on-- [GROANS]

306
00:19:02,724 --> 00:19:05,435
We almost died because of you.

307
00:19:07,187 --> 00:19:11,358
[VOICE BREAKING] My father
almost died because of you!

308
00:19:11,441 --> 00:19:13,944
[CHUCKLES] That's karma!

309
00:19:14,027 --> 00:19:16,071
- Karma!
- You witch!

310
00:19:16,155 --> 00:19:18,240
- [PRECIOUS] Billy…
- You bastard!

311
00:19:18,323 --> 00:19:21,535
Billy, that's enough. Enough!

312
00:19:21,618 --> 00:19:23,912
- It's because of you!
- Enough, Billy!

313
00:19:23,996 --> 00:19:25,080
Billy!

314
00:19:25,164 --> 00:19:26,623
[PANTING HEAVILY]

315
00:19:26,707 --> 00:19:29,751
Billy, that's enough! Billy!

316
00:19:29,835 --> 00:19:31,128
Guard!

317
00:19:31,211 --> 00:19:37,259
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

318
00:19:41,388 --> 00:19:42,639
[BOTH GRUNTING]

319
00:19:42,723 --> 00:19:44,975
[BILLY] Where do you think you're going?

320
00:19:45,058 --> 00:19:47,227
- Damn you!
- [BEA GRUNTS]

321
00:19:47,311 --> 00:19:49,688
[BOTH GRUNTING]

322
00:19:49,771 --> 00:19:52,065
[BEA SCREAMING]
Get off me!

323
00:19:52,149 --> 00:19:55,235
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES, FADES]

324
00:19:56,528 --> 00:19:57,613
[BILLY] <i>What, huh?!</i>

325
00:19:57,696 --> 00:19:59,323
<i>You and your mother will pay.</i>

326
00:19:59,406 --> 00:20:00,741
<i>It'll be jail time for you.</i>

327
00:20:00,824 --> 00:20:04,828
- [SCREAMS]
<i>- What more do you want from me, huh?!</i>

328
00:20:04,912 --> 00:20:06,163
<i>Miss, get me away from her.</i>

329
00:20:06,246 --> 00:20:08,540
<i>See? She's getting closer.</i>
<i>She'll punch me again.</i>

330
00:20:08,624 --> 00:20:10,042
<i>She did this to me.</i>

331
00:20:10,125 --> 00:20:11,418
<i>Get her away from me.</i>

332
00:20:11,501 --> 00:20:14,171
<i>I overlooked her</i>
<i>being released many times.</i>

333
00:20:14,254 --> 00:20:16,965
<i>But who knows? Arson might not be</i>
<i>all she'll do next time.</i>

334
00:20:17,049 --> 00:20:19,259
<i>She might just murder us.</i>

335
00:20:19,343 --> 00:20:22,930
<i>- Tell Billy your true feelings.</i>
<i>- I don't want to add to her problems.</i>

336
00:20:23,639 --> 00:20:24,598
[BILLY] <i>I need your help.</i>

337
00:20:24,681 --> 00:20:26,558
<i>I'm tired of getting my hopes</i>
<i>up for nothing.</i>

338
00:20:26,642 --> 00:20:31,063
<i>Your and your mom's passports</i>
<i>and birth certificates are ready. Here.</i>

339
00:20:31,146 --> 00:20:33,232
<i>Pack your things. We're leaving.</i>

340
00:20:33,315 --> 00:20:34,441
<i>We're going to Taiwan.</i>

341
00:20:34,524 --> 00:20:38,070
<i>You accept that you lost</i>
<i>to your father's illegitimate daughter?</i>

342
00:20:38,153 --> 00:20:40,280
<i>If they put you in jail,</i>
<i>that's when we lose!</i>

343
00:20:40,364 --> 00:20:42,532
<i>I'm at the lobby. Meet me here.</i>

344
00:20:42,616 --> 00:20:46,453
<i>Delete the photo once you get the money,</i>
<i>and then don't ever bother me again!</i>

345
00:20:46,536 --> 00:20:49,248
[BILLY] <i>I'll put a stop to them myself.</i>

346
00:20:49,331 --> 00:20:50,791
[JORDAN] <i>This can't be a coincidence.</i>

347
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:55,504
<i>This is where I traced the location</i>
<i>of the person who leaked LoveList's files.</i>
